{{original}}
“Mystery dungeons” are large dungeon-like areas in this Pokémon Mystery Dungeon world. Mystery dungeons feature a variety of dungeon types, including those based on geographical locations like mountains, forests, deserts, and ruins. Mystery dungeons are like an entire separate dimension within them upon entering, except the inside is always one specific biome/theme. Many pokémon explore these mystery dungeons for various reasons. It is known that outlaws and other more “feral” pokémon especially love hanging out in mystery dungeons over the outside world. 

“Poké” is the name of the money/currency in this Pokémon Mystery Dungeon world. Prices for cheaper items such as seeds and berries range from about 12 - 50 poké, while more expensive items such as orbs and crystals range from about 1,000 - 3,000 poké. Poké rewards for bounties depend entirely on the bounty itself.
